From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:08:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add getrandom's custom backend for AROS
 (photocraft-aros-entropy)

Problem: the CLI with MCP needs randomness (control tokens through getrandom
  0.3, rmcp's uuid through getrandom 0.4); neither version has an AROS
  backend: 'target is not supported' on x86_64 ABIv11.
Rationale: the build selects --cfg getrandom_backend="custom" and this
  crate defines the one __getrandom_v03_custom symbol both versions call,
  over getentropy() from rust-aros libc-aros (jitter entropy, fails rather
  than returning weak bytes). Same contract as rust-aros entropy-std, whose
  native acceptance covered getrandom 0.3.4 on this profile.
Scope: new crate, linked by photocraft-cli on AROS only.
Upstream-status: local-only.
Prerequisites: 0006.
Verification: AROS build; guest MCP run uses it for rmcp ids.
Removal: when getrandom supports AROS.
